-- title:
--   Branch prime with tangent X₀ detects mathfrak m_A-integral q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, assumed (hypothesis `hK`) to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb Q$-rational function field of $X_H$ of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/(q\ell))^\times$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as its fraction field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$; let $\varpi\in A$ satisfy $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$. Let $j\in K$ be an element, assumed non-zero through a `Fact` instance, whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Write $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout gluing $X_{\mathrm{fin}}=\mathrm{Spec}$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K j` (the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$) to the chart at infinity, and `toBase` for its structure morphism to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$.
--
--   Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak X$ and let $\varpi_z$ be (hypothesis `hϖz`) the germ at $z$ of the global function obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase`; it is assumed (`hz`) that $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$. Let $y$ be a point of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `ιFin` sending $y$ to $z$ (`hy`). The hypothesis `hss` requires $y$ to be supersingular in the following sense: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ (with decidable equality) and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ whose kernel is the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain and $\sigma:A\to W$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$. Let $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and with (hypothesis `hf`)
--   $$f-\bigl(X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1\bigr)\in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   the subtracted form being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18). Put $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma\varpi)\,v-f\,u\bigr)$ with quotient map $\mathrm{mk}_S$, and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}$ of the stalk onto $S$. Write $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion and $\mathrm{germ}_Y$ for the homomorphism from the chart algebra to the stalk given by identifying the chart algebra with the global sections of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$, transporting along `ιFin` and taking the germ at $z$ over the open image of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$.
--
--   Five groups of hypotheses are imposed on these data.
--
--   (`hconst`) Compatibility of $e$ with constants: for every $a\in A$, the image under $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$ of the germ at $z$ of $a$ (taken along `toBase`) is $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma a))$.
--
--   (`hfin`) Stability of the chart algebra: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, $\tau$ realises the action of $\gamma^{-1}$ on $K$ in the sense that for all weights $k$, all weight-$k$ forms $f_1,g_1$ on $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g_1$'s expansion non-zero, all $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the ratio of those expansions, and every embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the $\iota$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g_1\mid_k\gamma^{-1}$-conjugated-by-level equals that of $f_1\mid_k$ the same conjugate — the automorphism $\tau$ maps the chart algebra into itself.
--
--   (`hfix`) Fixing of the point $y$: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$, every $\tau$ as above for $\gamma^{-1}$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra, the induced endomorphism satisfies $\tau(a)-a\in y$ for every $a$ in the chart algebra.
--
--   (`hlin`) Equivariant linear parts: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau$ as above for $\gamma^{-1}$ which preserves the chart algebra and which fixes $y$ in the sense of the previous clause, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in\mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that: $\theta$ conjugates the action of $\tau$ on the chart algebra through $e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germ}_Y$; $\theta$ fixes every constant $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w))$, $w\in W$; for each index $j'$ one has $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S X_{j'})-\mathrm{mk}_S\bigl(\sum_{i}C(M_{ij'})X_i\bigr)$ in the square of the ideal of $S$ generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1}-1\in\mathfrak m_W$; $M_{ij'}-c\,\gamma_{ij'}\in\mathfrak m_W$ for all $i,j'$; if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then $c-1\in\mathfrak m_W$; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c-1\notin\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   (`hdist`) Separation of branches: for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ such that each $P_i$ fails to contain at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0,\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, contains $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and contains $\mathrm{mk}_S\bigl(C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1+h\bigr)$ for some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and such that $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct ideals of the stalk.
--
--   Conclusion. Let $P$ be a prime ideal of $S$ which does not contain at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0,\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, which contains $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and for which there is $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $\mathrm{mk}_S\bigl(C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h\bigr)\in P$, i.e. the branch through $P$ has tangent line $X_0$. Then for every $a$ in the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K j`,
--   $$\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y(a))\in e^{-1}(P)\iff \text{for every }n\in\mathbb Z\text{ there is }m\in\mathfrak m_A\text{ with }\bigl((a:K):\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L\bigr)\text{-coefficient at }n\text{ equal to }\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,L\,m,$$
--   where $e^{-1}(P)$ denotes the contraction of $P$ along $e$ to the completed stalk.
--
--   This supplies the branch-anchoring rider for the completed local chart of the integral model of $X_H$ at a supersingular point: among the $q+1$ branches of the Drinfeld–Igusa local equation $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ over $\sigma\varpi$, the one with tangent line $X_0$ is identified with the locus cut out by vanishing of all $q$-expansion coefficients modulo $\mathfrak m_A$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel), where the chart together with its equivariance and branch riders is assembled.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_forall_mem_comap_drinfeldChart_iff_forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel.lean

